From fb60828d71df7f328df0b2d39be9fff21d099fc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucius <chenyh572@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:04:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add optional animation of the cursor

Let the cursor be stretched between its old and its new position, with a
trail behind it, and shrink into the new one, instead of jumping there,
when 'cursor-animation-duration' is a number.  While it moves, the
cursor is not drawn in its new position, the terminal shows it, and when
the movement is over, Emacs draws the cursor and the terminal stops
showing it.  What moves and how is computed in xdisp.c, so that
terminals only have to show it; implement that on macOS and on PGTK.
The cursor on an image does not move like this.
The default duration is 0.1 seconds; setting it to nil disables animation.

* src/frame.h (struct cursor_glide): New struct.
(struct frame): New member 'cursor_glide'.
* src/dispextern.h (struct redisplay_interface): New member
'glide_cursor'.
(gui_cursor_glide_shape, gui_cursor_glide_progress)
(gui_cursor_glide_land): Declare.
* src/xdisp.c (glide_now, glide_ease_out, glide_corners)
(gui_cursor_glide_shape, gui_cursor_glide_progress, gui_glide_cursor)
(gui_cursor_glide_land): New functions.
(display_and_set_cursor): Call 'gui_glide_cursor'.
(syms_of_xdisp): Define 'cursor-animation-duration'.
* src/nsterm.h (EmacsView): New member 'cursorGlide'.
(EmacsView.cursorGlide): New method.
(EmacsCursorGlide): New class.
* src/nsterm.m (EmacsCursorGlide): Implement it.
(ns_glide_cursor): New function.
(ns_redisplay_interface): Use it.
(-[EmacsView dealloc]): Release 'cursorGlide'.
* src/pgtkterm.h (struct pgtk_output): New members 'glide_tick' and
'glide_timeout'.
* src/pgtkterm.c (pgtk_glide_stop, pgtk_glide_tick, pgtk_glide_land)
(pgtk_glide_cursor, pgtk_glide_path, pgtk_paint_glide): New functions.
(pgtk_redisplay_interface): Use 'pgtk_glide_cursor'.
(pgtk_handle_draw): Call 'pgtk_paint_glide'.
(pgtk_free_frame_resources): Call 'pgtk_glide_stop'.
* lisp/cus-start.el (standard): Add 'cursor-animation-duration'.
* doc/emacs/display.texi (Cursor Display): Document it.
* etc/NEWS: Announce it.
